#. Key:	Lore.01.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.01.Author"
msgid "Teodor Liss, dock master"
msgstr "Teodor Liss, dock master"

#. Key:	Lore.01.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.01.Body"
msgid "Jump day. Forty thousand colonists asleep in the holds, and the docks so quiet you can hear the Aether drive breathe through the hull. The Helios-Nadir observers came aboard at six with sealed orders and took the keys to the core vault themselves. Not one of my crew is cleared to open it any more. Captain Rhein says it is a formality. Formalities do not usually carry sidearms. At 11:40 the drive folds us past the edge of the Aether and out under a new sky. I have signed the last manifest. If anyone reads this: the docks were clean, the airlocks were green, and we were proud."
msgstr "Jump day. Forty thousand colonists asleep in the holds, and the docks so quiet you can hear the Aether drive breathe through the hull. The Helios-Nadir observers came aboard at six with sealed orders and took the keys to the core vault themselves. Not one of my crew is cleared to open it any more. Captain Rhein says it is a formality. Formalities do not usually carry sidearms. At 11:40 the drive folds us past the edge of the Aether and out under a new sky. I have signed the last manifest. If anyone reads this: the docks were clean, the airlocks were green, and we were proud."

#. Key:	Lore.01.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.01.Stamp"
msgid "Dock master's log, jump day"
msgstr "Dock master's log, jump day"

#. Key:	Lore.01.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.01.Title"
msgid "Day Zero"
msgstr "Day Zero"

#. Key:	Lore.02.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.02.Author"
msgid "Mara Okafor, deck C technician"
msgstr "Mara Okafor, deck C technician"

#. Key:	Lore.02.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.02.Body"
msgid "Third day since the jump and nobody on deck C has slept. Not won't. Can't. There is a hum under everything, as if the ship were thinking out loud. Petrov says it said his name in the ventilation shaft. Then I heard mine. This morning Kessler's eyes had gone white, milky, like frost on glass, and he kept working the welder as if he could still see. He said the light hurts now. He said the dark is warm. He whispered the rest and I couldn't hear it, but the others nodded. All of them at once."
msgstr "Third day since the jump and nobody on deck C has slept. Not won't. Can't. There is a hum under everything, as if the ship were thinking out loud. Petrov says it said his name in the ventilation shaft. Then I heard mine. This morning Kessler's eyes had gone white, milky, like frost on glass, and he kept working the welder as if he could still see. He said the light hurts now. He said the dark is warm. He whispered the rest and I couldn't hear it, but the others nodded. All of them at once."

#. Key:	Lore.02.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.02.Stamp"
msgid "Personal log, day 3 after the jump"
msgstr "Personal log, day 3 after the jump"

#. Key:	Lore.02.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.02.Title"
msgid "Whispers in the Vents"
msgstr "Whispers in the Vents"

#. Key:	Lore.03.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.03.Author"
msgid "Lt. Jonas Brandt, ship's security"
msgstr "Lt. Jonas Brandt, ship's security"

#. Key:	Lore.03.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.03.Body"
msgid "By order of the captain, docks A to F are sealed. No one passes the inner airlocks, crew or colonist, without a security escort. Anyone with white eyes, whispering or shying from light is to be held, not reasoned with. From this shift on, security wears reactor suits: the shielding keeps the hum out, or so Engineering says. Suits stay on for any reason. To eat. To sleep. We hold the locks until relieved. Brandt. P.S. The suits no longer come off easily. Ignore the rumours. Hold the locks."
msgstr "By order of the captain, docks A to F are sealed. No one passes the inner airlocks, crew or colonist, without a security escort. Anyone with white eyes, whispering or shying from light is to be held, not reasoned with. From this shift on, security wears reactor suits: the shielding keeps the hum out, or so Engineering says. Suits stay on for any reason. To eat. To sleep. We hold the locks until relieved. Brandt. P.S. The suits no longer come off easily. Ignore the rumours. Hold the locks."

#. Key:	Lore.03.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.03.Stamp"
msgid "Security order, day 9"
msgstr "Security order, day 9"

#. Key:	Lore.03.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.03.Title"
msgid "Lockdown Order No. 7"
msgstr "Lockdown Order No. 7"

#. Key:	Lore.04.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.04.Author"
msgid "Dr Ilse Varr, docks medical bay"
msgstr "Dr Ilse Varr, docks medical bay"

#. Key:	Lore.04.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.04.Body"
msgid "Forty-one admitted, forty-one blind. I have stopped writing names: they don't answer to them. They move together now, in clusters, through the service ducts, and when one of them flinches from my lamp, all of them do. The service biomass from the hydroponic vats is growing into them, or they into it; I can no longer tell which. They are not in pain. That is what frightens me. They whisper in their sleep, all of them the same words, and this morning I caught myself whispering along. Keep the lights on. Keep the lights on. Keep the"
msgstr "Forty-one admitted, forty-one blind. I have stopped writing names: they don't answer to them. They move together now, in clusters, through the service ducts, and when one of them flinches from my lamp, all of them do. The service biomass from the hydroponic vats is growing into them, or they into it; I can no longer tell which. They are not in pain. That is what frightens me. They whisper in their sleep, all of them the same words, and this morning I caught myself whispering along. Keep the lights on. Keep the lights on. Keep the"

