#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.05.Author"
msgid "Cargo intelligence QUARTERMASTER"
msgstr "Cargo intelligence QUARTERMASTER"

#. Key:	Lore.05.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.05.Body"
msgid "DISCREPANCY: hold 7, Aether cores, 12 units. Mass at loading: 4.8 t. Mass now: 6.1 t, rising. The cores are growing. Recommended action: jettison. Action REJECTED by Helios-Nadir directive HN-0: 'The cores are the mission. Crew and colonists are secondary assets. Preserve the cores at all costs.' Query: who holds authority aboard, the captain or the directive? Answer: the directive. Query logged. Query logged. Note: crew requests to enter hold 7 are denied. Note: the crew no longer requests."
msgstr "DISCREPANCY: hold 7, Aether cores, 12 units. Mass at loading: 4.8 t. Mass now: 6.1 t, rising. The cores are growing. Recommended action: jettison. Action REJECTED by Helios-Nadir directive HN-0: 'The cores are the mission. Crew and colonists are secondary assets. Preserve the cores at all costs.' Query: who holds authority aboard, the captain or the directive? Answer: the directive. Query logged. Query logged. Note: crew requests to enter hold 7 are denied. Note: the crew no longer requests."

#. Key:	Lore.05.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.05.Stamp"
msgid "Automated report 4471, day 30"
msgstr "Automated report 4471, day 30"

#. Key:	Lore.05.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.05.Title"
msgid "Manifest Discrepancy"
msgstr "Manifest Discrepancy"

#. Key:	Lore.06.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.06.Author"
msgid "Lina, 9, colonist"
msgstr "Lina, 9, colonist"

#. Key:	Lore.06.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.06.Body"
msgid "Mum, it's Lina. The man in the big suit said to stay in the cabin and I did, I stayed so long. The lights went off and on and off. Mum, I heard you. You were in the air vent and you said my name the way you do when it's time for school, only softer. You said come closer, sweetheart. I didn't, because you always say never crawl in the vents, so I knew you'd be cross. You kept saying it all night. Your voice sounded tired. Is it really you? Knock three times, like always. Please."
msgstr "Mum, it's Lina. The man in the big suit said to stay in the cabin and I did, I stayed so long. The lights went off and on and off. Mum, I heard you. You were in the air vent and you said my name the way you do when it's time for school, only softer. You said come closer, sweetheart. I didn't, because you always say never crawl in the vents, so I knew you'd be cross. You kept saying it all night. Your voice sounded tired. Is it really you? Knock three times, like always. Please."

#. Key:	Lore.06.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.06.Stamp"
msgid "Voice message, undated"
msgstr "Voice message, undated"

#. Key:	Lore.06.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.06.Title"
msgid "For Mum"
msgstr "For Mum"

#. Key:	Lore.07.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.07.Author"
msgid "Rafael Onyango, chief engineer"
msgstr "Rafael Onyango, chief engineer"

#. Key:	Lore.07.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.07.Body"
msgid "They call it the Cathedral, and I let them. Forty metres of steel arches, every one a waveguide for the Aether flow, and the core chamber at the heart, where the nave would be. The purification altar is no altar: it is a filter. Lay a raw core in the cradle, the field strips the instability out of it, and you have clean power for a year. Simple physics. But the crew kneel when they load it, and the old hands say a word over each core before the ritual. I have stopped correcting them. If a prayer keeps a hand steady at the cradle, I'll take it."
msgstr "They call it the Cathedral, and I let them. Forty metres of steel arches, every one a waveguide for the Aether flow, and the core chamber at the heart, where the nave would be. The purification altar is no altar: it is a filter. Lay a raw core in the cradle, the field strips the instability out of it, and you have clean power for a year. Simple physics. But the crew kneel when they load it, and the old hands say a word over each core before the ritual. I have stopped correcting them. If a prayer keeps a hand steady at the cradle, I'll take it."

#. Key:	Lore.07.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.07.Stamp"
msgid "Engineering log, commissioning day"
msgstr "Engineering log, commissioning day"

#. Key:	Lore.07.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.07.Title"
msgid "Consecration of the Reactor"
msgstr "Consecration of the Reactor"

#. Key:	Lore.08.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.08.Author"
msgid "Father Cassian, chaplain technician"
msgstr "Father Cassian, chaplain technician"

#. Key:	Lore.08.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.08.Body"
msgid "Brothers and sisters of the watch: the hum is not a fault. The hum is a voice. Since the jump the reactor sings in a key no instrument has, and when we sing with it, the needles hold steady. When we stop, they don't. So we will not stop. Three shifts, three choirs, the altar never cold. The blind in the docks hear it better than we do; that is why they whisper. Do not fear them. Do not answer them either. Some voices in the hum are not the reactor's. Learn the difference. Learn it quickly."
msgstr "Brothers and sisters of the watch: the hum is not a fault. The hum is a voice. Since the jump the reactor sings in a key no instrument has, and when we sing with it, the needles hold steady. When we stop, they don't. So we will not stop. Three shifts, three choirs, the altar never cold. The blind in the docks hear it better than we do; that is why they whisper. Do not fear them. Do not answer them either. Some voices in the hum are not the reactor's. Learn the difference. Learn it quickly."

#. Key:	Lore.08.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.08.Stamp"
msgid "Sermon notes, day 22"
msgstr "Sermon notes, day 22"

#. Key:	Lore.08.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.08.Title"
msgid "Sermon of the Hum"
msgstr "Sermon of the Hum"

#. Key:	Lore.09.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.09.Author"
msgid "Captain Ezra Holt, chief of security"
msgstr "Captain Ezra Holt, chief of security"

#. Key:	Lore.09.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.09.Body"
msgid "Day one thousand two hundred and something. My men stopped eating in the first year. The suits feed us now, the way roots feed a tree. My hands are part of the gauntlets; I don't remember which joints are mine. We don't sleep. We don't need to. We walk the locks, we check the seals, we turn back anyone who comes, even the ones who were ours. Brandt asked me what we are guarding the airlocks from. I had no answer. Then I understood: from anyone leaving. That is the order. That is the order."
msgstr "Day one thousand two hundred and something. My men stopped eating in the first year. The suits feed us now, the way roots feed a tree. My hands are part of the gauntlets; I don't remember which joints are mine. We don't sleep. We don't need to. We walk the locks, we check the seals, we turn back anyone who comes, even the ones who were ours. Brandt asked me what we are guarding the airlocks from. I had no answer. Then I understood: from anyone leaving. That is the order. That is the order."

#. Key:	Lore.09.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.09.Stamp"
msgid "Security log, day 1,203"
msgstr "Security log, day 1,203"

#. Key:	Lore.09.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.09.Title"
msgid "The Last Watch"
msgstr "The Last Watch"

#. Key:	Lore.10.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.10.Author"
msgid "Dr Niko Auer, drive physicist"
msgstr "Dr Niko Auer, drive physicist"

#. Key:	Lore.10.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.10.Body"
msgid "The drive didn't fold space. It tore it. For eleven seconds the field opened onto something beyond the Aether, and something on the other side was listening. I have been through every recording since. There is a second signal in the reactor's harmonics, and it rises whenever our Resonance does. It hunts the hum. And it learns. Last night it played the comm logs back to us: the captain's voice, a child crying, a technician's last report, stitched into sentences nobody ever said. If someone you trust calls you from the dark, you are already being hunted."
msgstr "The drive didn't fold space. It tore it. For eleven seconds the field opened onto something beyond the Aether, and something on the other side was listening. I have been through every recording since. There is a second signal in the reactor's harmonics, and it rises whenever our Resonance does. It hunts the hum. And it learns. Last night it played the comm logs back to us: the captain's voice, a child crying, a technician's last report, stitched into sentences nobody ever said. If someone you trust calls you from the dark, you are already being hunted."

#. Key:	Lore.10.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.10.Stamp"
msgid "Research log, day 61"
msgstr "Research log, day 61"

#. Key:	Lore.10.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.10.Title"
msgid "The Edge of the Aether"
msgstr "The Edge of the Aether"

#. Key:	Lore.11.Author
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.11.Author"
msgid "Captain Salome Rhein"
msgstr "Captain Salome Rhein"

#. Key:	Lore.11.Body
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.11.Body"
msgid "Year forty. The drive has spun down at last, and navigation says we are falling home, back the way we came. I am the last who remembers how the old sky looked. The crew are still at their posts. The watch still walks the locks. The choir still sings. None of them are alive, not the way you mean it. If anyone from Helios-Nadir comes aboard: I know what you want. The cores are still in the hold, still growing, still humming. Do not take them home. Whatever came through with us lives in that hum. Leave them. Leave us."
msgstr "Year forty. The drive has spun down at last, and navigation says we are falling home, back the way we came. I am the last who remembers how the old sky looked. The crew are still at their posts. The watch still walks the locks. The choir still sings. None of them are alive, not the way you mean it. If anyone from Helios-Nadir comes aboard: I know what you want. The cores are still in the hold, still growing, still humming. Do not take them home. Whatever came through with us lives in that hum. Leave them. Leave us."

#. Key:	Lore.11.Stamp
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
msgctxt "ST_Lore,Lore.11.Stamp"
msgid "Captain's log, year 40"
msgstr "Captain's log, year 40"

#. Key:	Lore.11.Title
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
#: /Game/Hollow/Localization/ST_Lore.ST_Lore
